      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 29-year-old male patient was involved in a crush injury of the right pelvis. Trauma screening showed a right-sided fracture of the pubic bone. CT imaging of the abdomen showed an urethral rupture with cranial displacement of the bladder, the so-called 'pie in the sky' sign."},
